Engine Simulator — https://github.com/ange-yaghi/engine-sim — MIT
Copyright 2022 AngeTheGreat (Ange Yaghi)

  The combustion engine simulation shipped as packages/enginesim/wasm/enginesim.wasm.
  With it, under the same MIT licence and the same copyright: piranha (the scripting
  language), simple-2d-constraint-solver (the rigid-body solver), and the engine
  definitions and impulse-response library embedded in that binary.

  We build against Open Engine Simulator (https://github.com/zabayone/open-engine-sim),
  the community fork, which is MIT and preserves the upstream notice. We do not
  modify any of it: the build fetches the pinned sources and links against them.
  Our own code in packages/enginesim — the C API, the audio worklet, the gearbox,
  the bench — is Apache-2.0.

  MIT requires the copyright notice and permission text to travel with the
  software. They do: packages/enginesim/wasm/LICENSE-engine-sim.txt ships beside
  the binary and is served with it, and CREDITS.md says what is inside.
